### Tested versions

godot 4.4 stable

### System information

Windows 11

### Issue description

When using the built-in Jolt Physics engine, Area3D does not consistently emit the BodyExited signal after a CharacterBody3D is removed from the scene tree, repositioned, and then re-added.

**Test logic**

A CharacterBody3D starts outside the Area3D.

It moves toward the Area3D using MoveAndSlide().

When it collides with the Area3D, the following happens in the BodyEntered handler:

The body is removed from the scene tree.

After 2 seconds, its position is reset.

The body is then re-added to the scene tree.

**Expected behavior (Godot Physics)**

First collision: BodyEntered → BodyExited.

After re-adding: BodyEntered immediately followed by BodyExited (clearing the cached overlap state).

This ensures consistent overlap tracking.

**Actual behavior (Jolt Physics)**

First collision: BodyEntered → BodyExited.

After re-adding: only BodyEntered is emitted.

BodyExited is never emitted again, leaving the body considered "stuck" inside the Area3D.

This results in inconsistent overlap detection.

### Steps to reproduce

```cs
public partial class Area: Area3D
{
    public override void _Ready()
    {
        BodyEntered += OnEnter;
        BodyExited += OnExit;   
    }
    bool once = false;
    void OnEnter(Node3D node)
    {
        GD.Print(1);
        if (once) return;
        once = true;
        GetTree().CreateTimer(2f).Timeout += () =>
        {
            node.Position = new Vector3(2f, 0, 0);
            var parent = GetParent();
            parent.AddChild(node);
        };
        GetParent().RemoveChild(node);
    }

    void OnExit(Node3D node)
    {
        GD.Print(2);
    }
}

public partial class Chr: CharacterBody3D
{
    public override void _PhysicsProcess(double delta)
    {
        Velocity = new Vector3(-0.5f, 0, 0);
        MoveAndSlide();
    }
}
```

Steps to reproduce:
Create an Area3D with Area.cs attached.
Add a CharacterBody3D with Chr.cs attached, outside the area, which will be moving towards the Area.
When the character enters the Area, it will be removed, repositioned, and re-added after 2 seconds.
Observe the console output.
Expected (Godot Physics):
1
2
1
2
Actual (Jolt Physics):
1
2
1

### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)

I think it’s easy to set it up the way I described.
